---
description: Interpret approved experiment outputs only after recovering the effective design and checking whether treatment changed measurement.
args: { question: ExperimentQuestion, bundle: ExperimentEvidenceBundle, prior?: ExperimentReviewCheckpoint | null }
returns: ExperimentReviewRun
uses: [experimentCore/frameExperimentQuestion, experimentCore/selectAnalysisPolicy, runCase/recoverDesign/orderPlanAmendments, runCase/auditMeasurement/checkMeasurementComparability, runCase/interpretResults/checkEstimandAndSearchHistory, runCase/reconcileFeedback/seekContraryExperience, experimentCore/deriveFollowupQuestions, experimentCore/collectReviewQuestions]
---
Bind saved = prior when supplied, otherwise null. Treat null as a first run; preserve all original task and evidence inputs.
1. Bind frame = frameExperimentQuestion(question) and policy = selectAnalysisPolicy(bundle.policies, question.experimentId). Preserve the named decision owner and meeting time as context; do not revise an earlier meeting without a supplied versioned decision record.
2. Bind timelines = for each review in bundle.reviews, orderPlanAmendments(review, bundle.plansAndAmendments). Reconstruct effective-time ordering, distinguish pre-outcome criteria from retrospective choices, and keep unresolved authorization or timing ambiguity visible.
3. Bind measurementAudits = checkMeasurementComparability(timelines, bundle.metricSchemasAndEvents, bundle.missingnessReports). Event-timing changes, missingness shifts, or schema changes invalidate affected windows before numerical outputs are interpreted.
4. Bind estimandChecks = for each output in bundle.analysisOutputs, checkEstimandAndSearchHistory(output, timelines, measurementAudits, bundle.approvedAnalyses, bundle.searchHistory). Require population, assignment unit, observation unit, outcome, uncertainty, multiplicity, approval reference and subgroup search history to match. Preserve an unapproved or mismatched output as unresolved rather than re-computing it.
5. Bind feedbackReviews = for each output and its matching estimand check, seekContraryExperience(estimandCheck, output, bundle.qualitativeAccounts). Withhold qualitative interpretation where approval, measurement or estimand gates fail. For an eligible output, preserve dissatisfied successes and satisfied failures; anecdote never becomes causal proof.
6. Bind followupQuestions = deriveFollowupQuestions(bundle.analysisOutputs, bundle.approvedAnalyses, bundle.followupSchemas, estimandChecks, measurementAudits). Confirmatory new-data work requires an eligible cohort, time window, allowed operation and completion test; missing design elements remain questions and blocked outputs do not inherit their measurement defect.
7. Bind questions = collectReviewQuestions(question.decisionOwnerId, timelines, measurementAudits, estimandChecks, followupQuestions). Derive exploratorySubgroups from analysis IDs marked exploratory by the checks and prohibitedPools from populations with failed assignment, outcome, approval or window checks.
8. Bind interpretation = { caseId: question.caseId, version: bundle.reviewVersion, decisionFrame: frame, applicablePolicy: policy, designTimelines: timelines, measurementAudits, estimandChecks, feedbackReviews, followupQuestions, exploratorySubgroups, prohibitedPools, questions, commitAllowed: false } as ExperimentInterpretation.
9. Bind changeImpact = compareReviewRevision(saved, interpretation). Reopen only analyses whose approved design, metric schema, missingness definition, subgroup search history or outcome receipt changed; keep unaffected complete analyses available.
10. Bind checkpoint = reconcileExperimentCheckpoint(saved, interpretation, changeImpact). Keep each interpretation edition and exact output identity; a later review never rewrites an earlier decision record or turns a follow-up question into collected data. Exact statistical calculation, approval, persistence and recommendation revision remain outside this source contract.
11. Return { interpretation, checkpoint, newlyInvalidatedAnalysisIds: changeImpact.newlyInvalidatedAnalysisIds, preservedAnalysisIds: changeImpact.preservedAnalysisIds, followupReopenedBy: changeImpact.followupReopenedBy } as ExperimentReviewRun. No completed effect is claimed.
